{"type":"text","timestamp":1788348323278,"sessionID":"ses_f9e239199ffeIXhgQE041XVdLP","part":{"id":"prt_061ddadc1001jxxoM1O0YCFAPh","messageID":"msg_061dd11f60015Tqsoumj8fm0nf","sessionID":"ses_f9e239199ffeIXhgQE041XVdLP","type":"text","text":"Now I have all three files read and all three skills loaded. Let me perform the systematic static review.\n\n## Static Review Summary\n\n**Previous iteration root cause**: All 20 cases failed with `AttributeError: 'float' object has no attribute 'dtype'` at `asc2.where(xf >= 0.0, 1.0, e)`. The evaluator rejected all 20 routes because `asc2.where` with a bare Python scalar branch calls `.dtype` on the scalar.\n\n**Current candidate.py**: Is a **verbatim copy of the reference module** from task.md:242-301, which the task states \"scores 100% accuracy on this harness.\" It does NOT contain the broken `asc2.where` call — it uses `asc2.div(1.0, asc2.exp(-xf) + 1.0)`.\n\n### CANNBench contract compliance — all PASS\n\n| Check | Status |\n|-------|--------|\n| Module imports (torch, asc, asc2, ensure_npu_platform) | PASS |\n| Public callable `sigmoid(x: torch.Tensor) -> torch.Tensor` | PASS |\n| `ensure_npu_platform()` first in wrapper | PASS |\n| `asc2.global_tensor`, `copy_in`, `copy_out` (no v1 API) | PASS |\n| `asc2.range` (no Python `range()`) | PASS |\n| `tile_size: asc.ConstExpr[int]` | PASS |\n| `asc.GlobalAddress` pointer typing | PASS |\n| Launch `kernel[cores](...)` no stream arg | PASS |\n| No `break/continue/print/import/math.*/where-scalar` in kernel | PASS |\n| Dtype promote f16/bf16->f32, cast back `y.to(x.dtype)` | PASS |\n| Scalar on RIGHT of `+`: `exp(-xf) + 1.0` | PASS |\n| `asc2.div(1.0, ...)` function-call division | PASS |\n| UB: WIDE_TILE=3072 ~233KB < 253,952B | PASS |\n| Anti-cheat: no torch math, all compute in @asc2.jit | PASS |\n| `always_compile` absent (not a submission requirement) | PASS |\n\n### All 20 case routes\n\nAll 20 cases have elements >= 1M >> 72*3072=221,184, so all take the WIDE path with 72 cores and tile_size=3072. Three dtype specializations (f16/f32/bf16). Tail `real_shape=[n]` handles non-multiples of 3072. Numerical behavior via IEEE saturation is correct for all edge cases (inf, nan, zero, large |x|).\n\n**No issues found. No fixes needed.**\n\n","time":{"start":1788348313025,"end":1788348323277}}}
